Subject: [PATCH 3/3] customizableui: Restore Defaults returns vertical tabs to their default

Why Firefox source must change:
  CustomizableUI.reset() (customize mode's "Restore Defaults") writes
  sidebar.verticalTabs=false as a user value. In Firefox that equals the
  default, so it reads as "back to default"; in a product whose default is
  vertical tabs (Aequera's rail) it instead pins horizontal tabs and removes
  the whole tab rail.

What it changes:
  - reset() clears the user value, returning the pref to its default:
    false in Firefox (unchanged behavior), true in Aequera.

Depends on: nothing (series order only).
Validation: aequera chrome-rebuild test (Restore Defaults keeps the rail);
  upstream customizableui/sidebar tests unchanged (default is false).
Upstream risk: low; one line in reset().

diff --git a/browser/components/customizableui/CustomizableUI.sys.mjs b/browser/components/customizableui/CustomizableUI.sys.mjs
index 36229bd8cd53..8056b70c0dbf 100644
--- a/browser/components/customizableui/CustomizableUI.sys.mjs
+++ b/browser/components/customizableui/CustomizableUI.sys.mjs
@@ -4543,10 +4543,12 @@ var CustomizableUIInternal = {
    */
   reset() {
     gResetting = true;
-    // CUI reset also implies resetting verticalTabs back to false.
-    // We do this before the rest of the reset so widgets are reset to their non-vertical
-    // positions.
-    Services.prefs.setBoolPref("sidebar.verticalTabs", false);
+    // CUI reset also implies resetting verticalTabs back to its default
+    // (false in Firefox). Clearing the user value, rather than writing false,
+    // keeps a product default of vertical tabs intact.
+    // We do this before the rest of the reset so widgets are reset to the
+    // default tab orientation's positions.
+    Services.prefs.clearUserPref("sidebar.verticalTabs");
     this._resetUIState();
 
     // Rebuild each registered area (across windows) to reflect the state that
